1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,660
In a time when many people around the globe are in lockdown and unable to attend the gym, emphasis has been placed on home exercising.
在全球许多人处于封锁状态、无法去健身房的时期，居家锻炼受到了重视。

2
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:21,780
Fears of a sedentary life and piling on the pounds are forcing many to find novel ways to move the body and stretch their muscles.
对久坐生活和体重增加的担忧，迫使许多人寻找新颖的方式来活动身体、拉伸肌肉。

3
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:29,760
You don’t need to pump iron or have expensive equipment like rowing and cycling machines to help you stay fit.
你不必举铁，也无需拥有划船机、健身单车这类昂贵器材，一样可以保持健康。

4
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:34,910
Exercising is not just important for your body, but also your mind.
锻炼不仅对身体有益，对心理也同样重要。

5
00:00:34,910 --> 00:00:49,940
A study by Dr. Andrea Dunn at the Cooper Research Institute in Dallas, Texas found patients who did daily 35-minute walks per week experienced a 47% reduction in their depression levels.
得克萨斯州达拉斯库珀研究所的安德里亚·邓恩博士开展的一项研究发现，每周坚持每天散步35分钟的患者，抑郁程度降低了47%。

6
00:00:49,940 --> 00:01:01,560
Cardiovascular exercise, often simply called cardio, is designed to keep your heart rate up, which in turn will strengthen your heart and improve your general fitness.
有氧运动通常简称为有氧训练，这类运动旨在提高心率，进而增强心脏功能、改善整体健康状况。

7
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:12,240
Many of us are turning to activities like skipping with an old rope, or watching one of the many ‘fitness experts’ who produce exercise videos online.
很多人开始选择一些简单的运动，比如用旧绳子跳绳，或是观看健身达人发布的线上锻炼视频。

8
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:17,980
Walking is another great aerobic activity to help you increase your blood circulation.
散步也是一项极佳的有氧运动，有助于促进血液循环。

9
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:28,510
There are many affordable pedometers which can be worn like a watch and used to track your steps, heart rate, sleeping patterns and even your blood oxygenation levels.
市面上有许多价格实惠的计步器，可像手表一样佩戴，用于记录步数、心率、睡眠模式甚至血氧饱和度。

10
00:01:28,510 --> 00:01:37,200
You don’t even have to step outside, with many simply power walking or jogging round their gardens or up and down their hallways.
你甚至不用出门，很多人就在自家花园里快走或慢跑，或是在走廊里来回踱步。

11
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:46,660
Practising yoga or Tai Chi can help to keep our bodies supple, which in turn can lower joint pain and help to protect us from injury.
练习瑜伽或太极有助于保持身体柔韧性，进而减轻关节疼痛、预防受伤。

12
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:56,860
Finally, strength and resistance training can be done at home by simply lifting bags of rice or boxes instead of heavy weights in the gym.
最后，力量和抗阻训练在家也能进行，不用去健身房举重物，只需举起几袋大米或几个箱子就行。

13
00:01:56,860 --> 00:02:07,090
There are many ways to help us stay mobile, and indeed these online exercise routines can be carried over in our lives long after lockdown is lifted.
保持身体灵活的方法有很多，而且这些线上锻炼方式，在封锁解除后的很长一段时间里都能继续存在于我们的生活中。

14
00:02:07,090 --> 00:02:18,920
For those of us who moan about our busy lives stopping us from hitting the gym, ten minutes a day with a rope or a bag of rice may not only help our fitness, but our mental health too.
对于那些抱怨工作太忙没时间去健身房的人来说，每天花十分钟跳绳或举米袋，不仅能增强体质，还能改善心理健康。
